@@ -9,6 +9,18 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+Visited page content stays mounted inside a persistent Astro container. Inactive
+views use `content-visibility: hidden` (with a `display: none` fallback), are inert,
+and are excluded from the accessibility tree. Navigation focuses the active main
+region without changing Astro's scroll restoration. The cache holds at most five
+views, including the active one, and evicts the least recently visited view.
+Paths and query strings identify views; hash fragments share the same view.
+Astro still fetches each destination and updates its head and shared page shell;
+return visits reuse cached content, including local form and component state.
+Reloading clears the cache and fetches fresh page content.
+
+Run `pnpm test` for automated DOM cache tests and `pnpm build` for the production build.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
